## Ontology Generate works across models and never fails the whole run for one bad page

Context:
On LGIT every Generate run failed (2026-10-27 and 2026-10-30, 4/4 traces in
/Shared/ontobricks-agents). `system.ai.claude-sonnet-5-5` on the AI Gateway
rejects `response_format` with "Structured output is not supported for this
model because its translation requires forced tool use, which newer
Anthropic models reject." That phrase was not recognised, so nothing was
retried; once stripped, the endpoint then rejects `temperature`, and only one
retry was allowed. Separately, upstream issue #173 (large table sets, wide
tables and large documents overflow the ~8k completion cap) is addressed by
upstream PR #206, which is still open.

Upstream PR applied:
- databrickslabs/ontobricks PR #206 "fix(agents): page stage-3 completion
  output to fit the completion cap" (head 03694b4f, author CactusQuill),
  cherry-picked unchanged as commit afa65589 (`git cherry-pick -x`). It adds
  `has_more` paging to relations / attributes / axioms, a smaller-page retry
  on truncation, a 16-page budget, SPEC/eval rows and its own changelog
  (changelogs/v0.9.0/Cactusquill_2026-10-24.log). Applied first so this fork
  stays aligned with upstream; the changes below sit on top of it.

Changes (this fork, on top of PR #206):
1. src/agents/engine_base.py
   - The unsupported-param matcher knows the structured-output phrase.
   - `call_serving_endpoint` strips and bans rejected params in a loop
     (response_format, then temperature) until the request is accepted,
     via the new `_strip_rejected_params` helper.
2. src/agents/llm_utils.py
   - `call_llm_with_retry` also retries HTTP 500/502/504 (was 429/503).
3. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py
   - `parse_json_object` extracts the first complete JSON object from a
     prose preamble or a fenced block when the answer is not pure JSON.
   - New `keep_closed_references`: resolves each entity reference (exact id,
     id without wrapping brackets/quotes, exact normalized label) within the
     closed set and drops items still outside, with one warning each.
4. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py
   - Each completion page is closure-filtered instead of rejected; dropped
     items are reported in `result["warnings"]`.
   - New `_keep_partial`: a page failing after earlier pages produced items
     (transport error, twice-truncated page, malformed page, page budget)
     ends the substage with those items plus a warning. Only a substage that
     produced nothing fails; malformed first-page output is still rejected.
   - Stage-1 finalization moved to `_finalize_detection` and gets ONE compact
     re-emission on `finish_reason=length`.
5. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py
   - New `build_compact_detection_retry_prompt`.
6. tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_robust_completion.py (new, 23 tests),
   tests/units/agents/test_agent_engine_base.py (+3),
   tests/units/agents/test_llm_utils.py (+3)
7. tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py
   - 8 tests moved to the new contract (dropped instead of rejected, bracketed
     id resolved, page budget keeps items, detection compact retry).
8. tests/eval/staged_contract.py, tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py,
   tests/eval/test_staged_contract.py, tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl,
   .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl
   - Kinds renamed: rejects_reference_to_excluded_entity -> drops_reference_to_excluded_entity,
     rejects_bracketed_id_reference -> resolves_bracketed_id_reference.
   - Rejection checks now use malformed output (the remaining rejection).
   - Rows staged-paged-attributes-page-budget-006 / -ghost-ref-007 expect kept items.
9. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md
   - Two §6 failure-mode rows and a §10 sign-off entry; documents the
     deliberate change from substage-level reject-only to item-level drop.
10. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   - Ratchet tightened (detect_entities 245 -> 191, _run_completion 119 -> 118,
     plus entries that had already shrunk).

